   <section class="card"><h2>Calculation methods</h2><p><code>Total return = (last − first) ÷ first × 100</code></p><p><code>Annualised volatility = std. dev. of daily returns × √252</code></p><p><code>Max drawdown = largest peak-to-trough decline within the window</code></p><p><code>Moving average = simple mean of the last n prices; trend compares the latest price with the average</code></p><p><code>Correlation = Pearson correlation between the two daily return series</code></p></section>
   <section class="card"><h2>Data & sources</h2><p>Analyses use the daily price history published on this site, not live market ticks.</p><p class="muted">Short windows give only an indicative result with lower reliability.</p><p class="muted"><strong>Data is for information only and is not investment advice.</strong> These tools show descriptive statistics only and are not investment advice.</p></section></main>
